            <li>Resoundant, Inc. <a href="https://www.fda.gov/media/143161/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Biomarker Qualification Letter of Intent: MR elastography liver stiffness</a>. Submitted to the FDA April 13, 2020.</li>
            <li>Wagner M, et al. <a href="https://pubs.rsna.org/doi/10.1148/radiol.2016160863" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Technical failure of MR elastography examinations of the liver: experience from a large single-center study</a>. Radiology, 2017;284(2):401–412.</li>
            <li>Serai SD, Pepin K, Chen J, Venkatesh SK, Obuchowski NA, Cole PE, Ehman RL; QMIC MRE Biomarker Committee. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1148/radiol.260974" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Standardizing Liver MR Elastography: Guidelines for Reliable Stiffness Measurement in Chronic Liver Disease</a>. Radiology, 2026;321(1).</li>
            <li>Mamidipalli A, Henderson WC, Hooker JC, et al. <a href="https://ismrm.gitlab.io/2018/2591.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Inter-reader agreement for liver magnetic resonance elastography region-of-interest (ROI) size, overlap, placement, and stiffness estimation in adults in a clinical trial</a>. ISMRM 2018, abstract 2591.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Contact title="Planning a liver study?" lede="Tell me about the indication, the endpoint and where you are in planning." />
  </main>
</Layout>
